## inspect {"kind": "howto", "query": "how to make selected text bold in LibreOffice Writer"} (10.8s) err=None imgs=[]
[inspect howto] (api:chat:deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017)
Select the text in LibreOffice Writer, then do one of:
• Press Ctrl+B (toggles bold; press again to unbold).
• Click the Bold “B” button on the Formatting toolbar.
• Use Format > Text > Bold.
For the full dialog: Format > Character > Font tab > Style: Bold > OK.
With no selection, Ctrl+B sets bold for text you type next.

